    "norm": "Tests how CharSet.getInstance() handles dash ('-') characters in unusual positions. The CharSet parser treats '-' as a range operator only when it appears between two non-dash characters (e.g. \"a-z\"). A dash that cannot form a valid range (at the start, end, or between two dashes) is treated as a literal character."
